  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for curl",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for curl fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-13608: flow in OpenLDAP SASL negotiation can cause an authentication bypass (bsc#1277476).\n- CVE-2026-80229: premature free can lead to OpenSSL provider use-after-free (bsc#1277479).\n- CVE-2026-80230: OpenSSL pinning bypass can allow unauthenticated connections to succeed (bsc#1277480).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
